From 5f5211a7c0387c987d0849e7e4393033dcd4eb63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@y>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:01:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] mptcp: cover the port-join announced-listener check on
 the SYN path

In subflow_check_req() the MP_JOIN SYN path had two sections: the token
lookup (keyed on the listener's msk, the target being unknown yet) and
the SYN-ACK thmac (keyed on the target). The announced-listener check
between them, subflow_use_different_sport() ->
mptcp_pm_announced_has_ssk(), which decides whether a join arriving on a
port the PM announced is admitted, ran outside both. It executes for
every port-join SYN (MPJoinPortSynRx counts it) and a coverage-guided
fuzzer read 0 PCs for it.

Start the target-keyed section right after the lookup instead of right
before the thmac, so the one section covers the port check and the thmac.
The check has a reject exit inside the section; it gets a matching stop.
The syncookie block that follows stays outside, as before.

Nesting check: the lookup section is closed before the new one opens;
mptcp_pm_announced_has_ssk() takes the PM spinlock and walks the
announce list, and subflow_req_create_thmac() computes the HMAC; neither
opens a section. The ACK-path twin of this check in
subflow_syn_recv_sock() is covered by that function's section.

Instrumentation-only, no functional change; no-op under CONFIG_KCOV=n.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PnC9KL4QuZ7vdAomuT6sTC
---
 net/mptcp/subflow.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/mptcp/subflow.c b/net/mptcp/subflow.c
index 200bebcc6a52..57fbfdf114c1 100644
--- a/net/mptcp/subflow.c
+++ b/net/mptcp/subflow.c
@@ -268,6 +268,12 @@ static int subflow_check_req(struct request_sock *req,
 			return -EPERM;
 		}
 
+		/* The join target is known from here on: one section keyed on
+		 * it over the port-join announced-listener check and the SYN-ACK
+		 * thmac.  Closed on the check's reject exit and after the thmac;
+		 * the syncookie block below keeps its own exits outside.
+		 */
+		mptcp_kcov_remote_start(subflow_req->msk);
 		if (subflow_use_different_sport(subflow_req->msk, sk_listener)) {
 			pr_debug("syn inet_sport=%d %d\n",
 				 ntohs(inet_sk(sk_listener)->inet_sport),
@@ -275,12 +281,12 @@ static int subflow_check_req(struct request_sock *req,
 			if (!mptcp_pm_announced_has_ssk(subflow_req->msk, sk_listener)) {
 				SUBFLOW_REQ_INC_STATS(req, MPTCP_MIB_MISMATCHPORTSYNRX);
 				subflow_add_reset_reason(skb, MPTCP_RST_EPROHIBIT);
+				mptcp_kcov_remote_stop(subflow_req->msk);
 				return -EPERM;
 			}
 			SUBFLOW_REQ_INC_STATS(req, MPTCP_MIB_JOINPORTSYNRX);
 		}
 
-		mptcp_kcov_remote_start(subflow_req->msk);
 		subflow_req_create_thmac(subflow_req);
 		mptcp_kcov_remote_stop(subflow_req->msk);
 
